{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Review financial support and respite care for unpaid carers",
        "additional_details": "We believe unpaid carers do not receive adequate support. Unpaid carers can face significant physical and emotional stress, carrying significant care responsibilities without sufficient financial support or access to respite care.\r\n \r\nWe believe carers should receive fair financial support without deductions, and have access to funded respite care that covers the person's care needs. We want the Government to review existing support and consider improvements.",
        "background": "We want the UK Government to review support for unpaid carers and disabled households, including access to funded respite care, financial support for carers, DWP assessments and benefit deductions. We want the Government to consider urgent reform to improve support for carers. ",
